    {
        "content": "<p>There is an implementation of effects on github: <a href=\"https://github.com/palladin/lean-eff/\">lean-eff</a>.</p>",
        "id": 615487045,
        "sender_full_name": "Daniil Kisel",
        "timestamp": 1786298685
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Yes i tested it. It does not have the extensibility of ZIO. you need to implement an Effect that need to comply to an interface. It's too much to ask for proper effects as this requires every effect to be effectified into the library semantics. That's a show stopper for me.<br>\nThe example showned above don't require anything from the user. You can implement config and logger however you want. You can actually use any type as an effect.<br>\nThis lowers the barrier to entry and match what ZIO and Effect.Ts tries to achieve.</p>",
        "id": 615488852,
        "sender_full_name": "Alfredo Moreira-Rosa",
        "timestamp": 1786300358
    }
]